## Verdict
B8 list binds are on disk. The seven typecheck bind sites use `list_push`, not `binds = binds +`. `drop_depth` uses `str_ends_with`. `scope_has` compares `name@d`. The root-cause audit names `env.oo` a red herring and records 50 s / 30 GB → 28.5 s / 12 GB, not a 39 MB close.

| Check | Status | Live evidence |
|-------|--------|---------------|
| (1) `list_push`, not string concat on binds | **PASS** | 7 sites + extra_binds split; `binds = binds +` = 0 in these two files |
| (2) `drop_depth` uses `str_ends_with` | **PASS** | `tc_scope.oo:45` |
| (3) `scope_has` `name@d` | **PASS** | `tc_scope.oo:23` needle `name + "@" + d.to_string()` |
| (4) audit does not say `env.oo` was the B8 fix | **PASS** | culprit = `tc_names.oo` + `tc_scope.oo`; `env.oo` = RED HERRING |
| (5) honest metrics 50 s / 30 GB → 28.5 s / 12 GB, not 39 MB | **PASS** | table + §5 + §8; 39 MB named as unrecovered other-ELF baseline |
| Sprint line map 47/76/… | **NOTE** | live lines shifted; sites still present |
| `list_filter` wording | **NOTE** | inlined O(K) loop, same job |
| Residual 12 GB / not 1–2 s / 39 MB | **PASS** | residual §7; B6+B7 still open on the board |

Overall: **PASS**. No product flag.

## 1. `list_push` not string concat
`typecheck_undefined_vars_ext` types `binds` as `List[String]` (`tc_names.oo:27`). Comment at 14–15 states the old String churn was 30 GB / 50 s.

Ripgrep `binds = binds` in `tc_names.oo` and `tc_scope.oo`: **zero**.

Seven bind-append sites (sprint cited 47, 76, 94, 113, 122, 140, 147 — those numbers are stale; live file grew a header):

| Role | Live | Code |
|------|-----:|------|
| fn-name pre-bind | 55 | `binds = list_push(binds, fname + "@0")` |
| KW_LET | 84 | `binds = list_push(binds, vname + "@" + ds)` |
| param / struct field | 102 | `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)` |
| Ok/Err/Some | 121 | `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)` |
| FATARROW | 130 | `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)` |
| KW_FOR | 148 | `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)` |
| legacy IDENT `for` | 155 | `binds = list_push(binds, name + "@" + ds)` |

Two more `list_push` sites (35, 44) split `extra_binds` on tab. API stays a String; list form starts at function entry. Fine.

`name + "@" + ds` still allocates a small String per bind. That is payload, not the old whole-`binds` concat.

Out of B8 files: `ooda/oodac/check_scan.oo:178,187` still does `binds = binds + cur + "@0\t"` inside `names_to_depth0_binds` (String extra_binds builder). Not the typecheck accumulator. Not a B8 FAIL.

## 2. `drop_depth` uses `str_ends_with`
Live `tc_scope.oo:36-51` (sprint said 28-43).

- Input/output: `List[String]`.
- Marker: `"@" + depth.to_string()`.
- Keep test: `if !str_ends_with(e, marker)` then `out = list_push(out, e)`.
- No `contains` / mid-string scan of the bind entry.

Sprint text said `list_filter`. Live code is the same O(K) rebuild, written as a while loop. Not a call to `list_filter`. Same cost class as claimed. Wording drift only.

Old anti-pattern (full String rebuild of one `binds` blob) is gone.

## 3. `scope_has` `name@d`
Live `tc_scope.oo:19-34` (sprint said 11-26).

```
let needle = name + "@" + d.to_string();
if list_get(binds, i) == needle { return true; }
```

`d` walks `0 ..= max_depth`. Entries are `"name@depth"`. Lookup is exact list-slot compare, not tab-wrapped substring on one big String.

`binds_has` (`tc_scope.oo:12-15`) still does `"\t" + name + "\t"` on a String. That is the type-env table, not the scoped bind list. Untouched by the B8 list conversion. Out of this check.

## 4. Audit does not say `env.oo` was the B8 fix
`openOODA/audit/b8_root_cause.oot`:

- Verdict table: root cause = **`tc_names.oo` + `tc_scope.oo`**. `env.oo` culprit = **RED HERRING**.
- §1 title: "Red herring — `env.oo` is fine (PV2 confirms)".
- §4 title: "Fix — list-based binds (applied)".
- Cross-ref L139: `env.oo:6` is `return oo_env_get(cap, key);` **(the fix; NOT the cause)**.

"The fix" on L119 / L139 is the B5 self-call close (`oo_env_get`), not the B8 allocator patch. The doc does **not** claim `env.oo` closed the 30 GB / 50 s check. It says the opposite.

This turn did not re-run PV2.

## 5. Metrics: 50 s / 30 GB → 28.5 s / 12 GB, not 39 MB
From `b8_root_cause.oot` (not re-timed here):

| Claim | Present? | Where |
|-------|----------|-------|
| Pre ≈ 50 s / 30 GB | YES | L15–16, L83–84 (50.4 s ± 1.2 s / 30.8 GB, PV1 n=5) |
| Post 28.5 s / 12 GB | YES | L15–16, L83–84, L126 |
| Δ 1.77× wall / 2.5× RSS | YES | L83–84, L91, L128 |
| 1.7 s / 41 MB fabricated | YES | L20, L123 (DOCS v1 inflated; corrected) |
| 1–2 s / 39 MB **not** the post-patch number | YES | L19, L91, L113–114 (other ELF `10e9128a…`; **NOT recovered**) |

The audit does **not** report the list-binds patch as 39 MB. 39 MB is the old 02:14 baseline, named as residual debt.

This verify did not clock `oodac check oodac/main.oo`. Numbers are inherited from the corrected root-cause doc + the board.

